.TH HD-YAZI 1 "October 2026" "yazi" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-yazi \- start yazi where it was left the last time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-yazi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-yazi
starts
.BR yazi ,
the terminal file manager, in the directory it was in when it quit the last
time.
yazi writes that directory to the state file when it quits, through its
option
.BR \-\-cwd\-file .
.PP
Without a state file, or when the directory in it no longer exists, yazi
starts in the home directory.
The state file is per user.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/yazi/last-cwd
The last directory of yazi; without
.BR XDG_STATE_HOME ,
.IR ~/.local/state/yazi/last-cwd .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of yazi, or 1 when yazi cannot be started.
